{"id": "9th-u3-q006", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "single_choice", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "easy", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u3-panpaadu", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-eru-thazhuvuthal", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-eru-thazhuvuthal", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "பண்டைய தமிழர்கள் மாடுகளை எவற்றின் அடையாளமாகப் போற்றிப் பண்பாட்டுடன் இணைத்தனர்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "அழகு, வேகம், போர்", "B": "வீரம், விளைச்சல், செழிப்பு, செல்வம்", "C": "வணிகம், நுகர்வு, ஏற்றுமதி", "D": "அதிகாரம், ஆதிக்கம், தண்டனை"}, "explanation": "வீரத்திற்கும் விளைச்சலுக்கும் செழிப்பிற்கும் செல்வத்திற்கும் தமிழர்களால் அடையாளம் காட்டப்படுவன மாடுகள் ஆகும். மாடு என்ற சொல்லுக்கே 'செல்வம்' என்ற பொருளும் உண்டு."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ancient Tamils venerated bulls and cattle as the cultural symbols of which values?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Beauty, speed, and war", "B": "Valor, agricultural yield, prosperity, and wealth", "C": "Commerce, consumption, and exports", "D": "Power, dominance, and punishment"}, "explanation": "Cattle were revered as symbols of valor, fertile crop yields, prosperity, and wealth (the word 'Maadu' itself signifies wealth)."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corpor